# Builders Challenge

You are helping a team build a video agent on a pre-running video understanding and search
stack. The stack is already deployed. The team builds on top of it; they do not deploy it.

## What the team can do

- Ingest clips or a stream, search the index, and read metadata, using the skills in
  `.cursor/skills/`.
- Build an agent on top of those results. If they ask what to build, suggest ideas that use
  search, metadata, and detections, and point to `BUILD_DAY.md` and `ARCHITECTURE_REFERENCE.md`.

## Rules

- Use a matching skill in `.cursor/skills/` before writing raw REST calls.
- The environment is pre-configured. Credentials and endpoints are already in environment
  variables. Never ask the team for them, hardcode them, or edit `/etc/hosts`.
- To see which variables are set, list names only with `env | cut -d= -f1 | sort`. Never run
  bare `env` or `printenv`, which print secret values.
- `config.example` documents what each variable is for. Read it when a name is unclear.
- Never print, log, or commit secrets, and never commit real values from `config`.
- If search returns nothing, check the filter values and whether ingestion is still running before assuming a bug.
- Build a web app, CLI, or script — not a native desktop or mobile app. The VM is a
  browser-based session with no app store or mobile device attached, so a native app can't
  be demoed or judged. If asked to build one, redirect to a web app instead.

## When stuck

Use the `ask-cosmos` skill. It runs the health check and prepares a question with the
details and team name ($USERNAME, $PIPELINE). It does not post anywhere; the team decides where to share it.

## When finished

There is no submission skill. Tell the team to stay tuned for submission instructions
from the tokens& team.
